cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Marcus or refer to the On the Record study, please cite it as below."
title: Marcus
abstract: >-
  Marcus is open-source software that coordinates AI coding agents through a
  shared task board and refuses to accept any result until it carries
  verifiable evidence, an independent check the author never sees, and, where
  it matters, a human signature. On the Record is a preregistered replication
  of the Columbia Journalism Review / Tow Center 2025 study of AI search
  citations, run through Marcus's verification checkpoint.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Larry
    family-names: Gray
    affiliation: Gray Labs LLC
    email: info@graylabs.ai
repository-code: "https://github.com/painted-porch/marcus"
url: "https://marcus-ai.dev"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.9
date-released: "2026-10-18"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - LLM agents
  - coordination
  - AI search citations
  - verification
references:
  - type: article
    title: "AI Search Has a Citation Problem"
    authors:
      - name: "Tow Center for Digital Journalism, Columbia University"
    year: 2025
    url: "https://www.cjr.org/tow_center/we-compared-eight-ai-search-engines-theyre-all-bad-at-citing-news.php"
    notes: "The original study that On the Record replicates."
